+MAKUENI WARD BACKFILL (24 Oct 2026)
+
+Why: the dashboard, segments and Constituent Database only count a contact in a
+ward when its ward is one of the 30 official names (e.g. "Kako/Waia"). Contacts
+from the 21 Oct import were left with no ward whenever the import flagged any
+issue, and spellings like "KEE WARD" or "Waia-Kako" were not recognised.
+
+1. In Supabase, open the Makueni project used by Render's DATABASE_URL.
+2. SQL Editor: paste 00_preview_ward_backfill.sql and Run. It changes nothing.
+   Read the two result tables: how many records would change, and the ward
+   totals afterwards.
+3. If the numbers look right, paste 01_ward_backfill.sql and Run once.
+4. Reload the dashboard. Contacts still under "(no ward)" or "(not an official
+   ward: ...)" need a person to review them in the Constituent Database.
+
+Undo: every changed row's previous ward/sub_county is in
+public.makueni_ward_backfill_backup_20261024 (columns id, ward, sub_county).
